OL,3,GNEWSAGirls fear real life consequences 
OL,4,Aof misogyny                            
OL,6,FGirls as young as 13 have said         
OL,7,Fmisogynistic behaviour has become so   
OL,8,F"normalised" they are no longer        
OL,9,Fsurprised by it and fear it will never 
OL,10,Fchange.                                
OL,12,FSharing their experiences at a         
OL,13,Fconference in Sunderland organised by a
OL,14,Fdomestic abuse charity, they said boys 
OL,15,Fwould call them sexualised names and   
OL,16,Fcomment on their bodies but they felt  
OL,17,Funcomfortable in challenging this.     
OL,19,FSome boys at the event said they might 
OL,20,F"make jokes" but had not realised the  
OL,21,Fimpact this had.                       
